        "original_id": "09a08553-2b7d-5c0d-a62c-114ab2cc993d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pablo Trapero, Aleksander Ford\n- Films: Crane World\n- Roles: film producer, editor, director, head of the Polish People's Army Film Crew\n- Places: Argentina, Kiev, Russian Empire, Naples, Florida, United States, Soviet Union\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Aleksander Ford was born as Mosze Lifszyc on 24 November 1908 in Kiev in the Russian Empire.\n- Pablo Trapero was born on 4 October 1971 and is an Argentine film producer, editor, and director.\n- During World War II, Aleksander Ford served as head of the Polish People's Army Film Crew in the Soviet Union.\n- Crane World, or Mundo grúa in Spanish, is a 1999 Argentine film written and directed by Pablo Trapero.\n- Aleksander Ford was a Polish Jewish film director.\n- Aleksander Ford died on 4 April 1980 in Naples, Florida, United States.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
